b/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563700 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(-4,1)$\n\nII. $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$\n\nIII. $(0,1)\\cup (7,9]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563700 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e1139bd-70c8-5172-a11e-474495b10da9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563700 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-4,1)$ and $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$ are open because:\n\n- The boundary points of the set $(-4,1)$ are $-4$, and $1.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of the set  $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$ are $2$, $4$, $5$, and $6.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not open because $(0,1)\\cup (7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $1$, $7$, and $9$, and the point $9$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563734 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186563603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563734 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563734 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563734 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $[0,15]$\n\nII. $(-3,5]\\cup [6,8)$\n\nIII. $(1,6)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7bf2d22-67db-5bfb-9d76-d999020db50d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186563734 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(1,6)$ is open. The boundary points are $1$, and $6.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $[0,15]$ has two boundary points $0$, and $15$, and both of them lie in the set.\n\n- $(-3,5]\\cup [6,8)$ has four boundary points $-3$, $5$, $6$, and $8$, and the points $5$ and $6$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
